<title>JAPAN: NTT to cut long-distance rates 20-30 yen.</title>
<headline>NTT to cut long-distance rates 20-30 yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Telegraph and Telephone Corp (NTT) said on Friday it plans to cut domestic long-distance call rates by 20 to 30 yen from the current 140 yen per three minutes, possibly as early as next February.</p>
<p>It plans to apply for permission to make the rate cut to the Posts and Telecommunications Ministry in December, NTT president Junichiro Miyazu told a news confernece.</p>
</text>
